@*
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  User (non-admin) page template — copy this file to create a new routable page
  for signed-in users. Not linked from NavMenu. Open directly, e.g.:
  https://localhost:5001/user/dev/page-template
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Checklist when copying:
  - Rename the file and set a unique @page route (e.g. @page "/user/your-feature").
  - Keep [Authorize] as below for any authenticated user, or add a policy / roles
    if you need stricter access than the app-wide fallback policy.
  - Catalog-driven “help” pages usually live under /app/{appId}/page/{pageId} — see
    Support/ApplicationPage.razor. Use this template for standalone user tools or experiments.
  - Inject HelpDeskDbContext, services, and IJSRuntime as needed; match patterns
    in Support/Dashboard.razor or Support/ApplicationPage.razor for consistency.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*@

@page "/user/dev/page-template"

@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>User page template</PageTitle>

<div class="hd-admin-page">
    <h1>New user page</h1>
    <p class="muted">Duplicate this file, change the <code>@@page</code> route, and replace this content. This template is not in the sidebar.</p>
    <div class="hd-card">
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0;">Placeholder — add your UI here.</p>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
}
